<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karabakh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qarabagh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karabakh is a region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-caucasus">South Caucasus</a>, between the Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> mountains and the Kura and Aras rivers, today in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>. Its highlands, long home to Armenian princes and meliks, and its lowland pastures were ruled in turn by Persian, Turkic and local dynasties, then by the Karabakh Khanate and, from 1805, by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It was fought over in 1988–1994 and 2020, and Azerbaijan took control of the whole region in 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karabakh.jpg" alt="Karabakh" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LJ user plusninety · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karmir-shuka.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
